<title>UK: Japanese stocks edge higher in London.</title>
<headline>Japanese stocks edge higher in London.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese stocks in London rose mildly in quiet trade on Monday with bank and export stocks attracting the most interest, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're having a slightly better day. This morning there was buying interest in the bank sector, which had a good move overnight,&quot; a London-based trader said. &quot;The dollar's strength today also encouraged some buying of export-related issues.&quot;</p>
<p>Sumitomo Bank and Mitsui Trust showed strong support, with Sumitomo edging higher from its Tokyo close to 1,580 yen and Mitsui up to 755 yen.</p>
<p>The Nikkei/ISE 50 index rose to 1,419.93, up 10.88 points from its previous London close. Earlier in Tokyo the benchmark Nikkei 225 average gained 153.83 points to 18,267.72.</p>
<p>-- Scott McCormack, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
